e":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3695","lemma":"כַּסְלֻחִים","tr":"kas·lu·chim","gloss":"Casluhim","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Ham, the father of Canaan, saw his fatherʼs nakedness and told his two brothers outside.","from":13},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":25,"verseEnd":26,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"he said, “Cursed be Canaan! A servant of servants shall he be to his brothers.” He also declared: “Blessed be the Lord, the God of Shem! May Canaan be the servant of Shem.","from":13},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":1,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"This is the account of Noahʼs sons Shem, Ham, and Japheth, who also had sons after the flood. The sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras. The sons of Gomer: Ashkenaz, Riphath, and Togarmah. And the sons of Javan: Elishah, Tarshish, the Kittites, and the Rodanites. From these, the maritime peoples separated into their territories, according to their languages, by clans within their nations.","from":5},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Gomer: Ashkenaz, Riphath, and Togarmah.","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Ham: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":6,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Ham: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan. The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabtah, Raamah, and Sabteca. And the sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabtah, Raamah, and Sabteca. And the sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan.","from":9},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":8,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Cush was the father of Nimrod, who began to be a mighty one on the earth. He was a mighty hunter before the Lord; so it is said, “Like Nimrod, a mighty hunter before the Lord.” His kingdom began in Babylon, Erech, Accad, and Calneh, in the land of Shinar. From that land he went forth into Assyria, where he built Nineveh, Rehoboth-Ir, Calah, and Resen, which is between Nineveh and the great city of Calah.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"17-27":{"people":[{"id":"arpachshad-h0775","name":"Arpachshad","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":3,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"shem-h8035","name":"Shem","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Noah","count":2,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"aram-h0758g","name":"Aram","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"asshur-h0804h","name":"Asshur","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"elam-h5867c","name":"Elam","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"gether-h1666","name":"Gether","kind":"person","brief":"Early Patriarch","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"hul-h2343","name":"Hul","kind":"person","brief":"Early Patriarch","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"lud-h3865","name":"Lud","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"mash-h4851","name":"Mash","kind":"person","brief":"Grandson of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"uz-h5780g","name":"Uz","kind":"person","brief":"Grandson of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"eber-h5677g","name":"Eber","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shelah","count":3,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"shelah-h7974","name":"Shelah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Cainan","count":2,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"joktan-h3355","name":"Joktan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Eber","count":3,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"peleg-h6389","name":"Peleg","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Eber","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"almodad-h0486","name":"Almodad","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joktan","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"hazarmaveth-h2700","name":"Hazarmaveth","kind":"person"