ang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":12},{"base":"H8478","lemma":"תַּחַת","tr":"ta·chat","gloss":"underneath: under","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":505},{"base":"H8555","lemma":"תִּמְנָע","tr":"tim·na","gloss":"Timna","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":6},{"base":"H3877","lemma":"לוֹטָן","tr":"lo·tan","gloss":"Lotan","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":7},{"base":"H6034","lemma":"עֲנָה","tr":"a·nah","gloss":"Anah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":12}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":36,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When Baal-hanan son of Achbor died, Hadad reigned in his place. His city was named Pau, and his wifeʼs name was Mehetabel daughter of Matred, the daughter of Me-zahab.","from":50},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Aram: Uz, Hul, Gether, and Mash.","from":42},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab. All these were sons of Joktan.","from":45},{"book":"GEN","chapter":16,"verse":11,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The angel of the Lordproceeded: “Behold, you have conceived and will bear a son. And you shall name him Ishmael, for the Lordhas heard your cry of affliction. He will be a wild donkey of a man, and his hand will be against everyone, and everyoneʼs hand against him; he will live in hostility toward all his brothers.” So Hagar gave this name to the Lordwho had spoken to her: “You are the God who sees me,” for she said, “Here I have seen the One who sees me!” Therefore the well was called Beer-lahai-roi. It is located between Kadesh and Bered. And Hagar bore Abram a son, and Abram gave the name Ishmael to the son she had borne.","from":28},{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":19,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But God replied, “Your wife Sarah will indeed bear you a son, and you are to name him Isaac. I will establish My covenant with him as an everlasting covenant for his descendants after him. As for Ishmael, I have heard you, and I will surely bless him; I will make him fruitful and multiply him greatly. He will become the father of twelve rulers, and I will make him into a great nation. But I will establish My covenant with Isaac, whom Sarah will bear to you at this time next year.”","from":28},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":2,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Sarah conceived and bore a son to Abraham in his old age, at the very time God had promised. And Abraham gave the name Isaac to the son Sarah bore to him. When his son Isaac was eight days old, Abraham circumcised him, as God had commanded him. Abraham was a hundred years old when his son Isaac was born to him.","from":28},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":2,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Sarah conceived and bore a son to Abraham in his old age, at the very time God had promised. And Abraham gave the name Isaac to the son Sarah bore to him.","from":34},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":9,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But Sarah saw that the son whom Hagar the Egyptian had borne to Abraham was mocking her son, and she said to Abraham, “Expel the slave woman and her son, for the slave womanʼs son will never share in the inheritance with my son Isaac!”","from":28}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":5}]}}